<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
        This theme styles almost nothing — Compose M3 draws every pixel of real UI, and ADR-0012
        keeps visual design in its own phase. What it does decide is the window: no action bar, and
        a parent an AppCompatActivity will accept.

        That parent is not a style preference, it is a hard requirement of ADR-0013's language
        switcher: AppCompatActivity throws on a theme that does not descend from Theme.AppCompat.
        It is deliberately *not* a Material Components theme (Theme.MaterialComponents.*) — that
        would pull in com.google.android.material, a second widget library rendering nothing, when
        AppCompat's own theme is all the activity asks for.

        DayNight makes the window background follow the system dark-mode setting, which keeps the
        pixels Android owns — the window background, the frame drawn before Compose composes — in
        step with the colour scheme Theme.kt picks from isSystemInDarkTheme().
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Binky" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar" />
</resources>